% Test cases for the immunosuppressive drugs policy (immunosuppressive_drugs.le):
% synthetic claims, one or two per criterion of Policy Article A52474 and of
% LCD L33824, each stating only what its record shows. The diagnosis is a
% code of the article's ICD-10 table. The queries: whether the claim is
% payable (the first query, so "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is
% reasonable and necessary, and what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base immunosuppressive drugs cases includes these resources:
    immunosuppressive_drugs.

the knowledge base immunosuppressive drugs cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for a 90-day supply of tacrolimus (J7507) after a kidney
% transplant (Z94.0): every criterion and every documentation requirement in
% the record; the drug is furnished on the day of discharge.
scenario tacrolimus_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the tacrolimus.
    the HCPCS code of the tacrolimus is "J7507".
    the tacrolimus is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "Z94.0".
    Ann received a transplant of kidney on 2026-02-20.
    the transplant of Ann met the Medicare coverage criteria in effect at the time.
    Ann was enrolled in Medicare Part A at the time of the transplant.
    Ann is enrolled in Medicare Part B at the time the drugs are dispensed.
    Ann was discharged from the hospital following the transplant on 2026-03-01.
    the labeling of the tacrolimus includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ.
    the finding regimen necessary to prevent rejection about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "tacrolimus 4 mg twice daily, the standard maintenance regimen after kidney transplantation".
    the supplier holds the transplant date of Ann obtained from the treating practitioner.
    the order for the tacrolimus is dated 2026-02-27.
    the order for the tacrolimus is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the tacrolimus includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the tacrolimus includes order date.
    the order for the tacrolimus includes description of the item.
    the order for the tacrolimus includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the tacrolimus includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the tacrolimus was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-27.
    the tacrolimus was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the tacrolimus.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% Mycophenolate for rheumatoid arthritis (M06.9), no transplant: not
% reasonable and necessary.
scenario non_transplant_diagnosis is:
    claim 1 is for the mycophenolate.
    the HCPCS code of the mycophenolate is "J7517".
    the mycophenolate is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Ben is "M06.9".
    the labeling of the mycophenolate includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ.
    the finding regimen necessary to prevent rejection about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% A pancreas transplant alone (Z94.83, 2024): Cy meets the criteria of
% I(E) (a Medicare-approved facility, type I diabetes, a positive
% autoantibody test, the labile diabetes, 18 months under an
% endocrinologist, the two findings); Dee had the same transplant with no
% autoantibody test and a fasting C-peptide at 150 percent of the lower
% limit of normal — not a qualifying transplant.
scenario pancreas_alone is:
    claim 1 is for the tacrolimus.
    the HCPCS code of the tacrolimus is "J7507".
    the tacrolimus is furnished to Cy.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the diagnosis code of Cy is "Z94.83".
    Cy received a transplant of pancreas alone on 2024-05-10.
    the transplant of Cy was performed in a facility that is Medicare approved for kidney transplantation.
    the medical record of Cy documents type I diabetes.
    the beta cell autoantibody test of Cy is positive.
    the medical record of Cy documents labile insulin dependent diabetes with hospitalization.
    Cy was under the care of an endocrinologist with optimal and intensive management for 18 months.
    the finding able to manage lifelong immunosuppression about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding suitable candidate for transplantation about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the transplant of Cy met the Medicare coverage criteria in effect at the time.
    Cy was enrolled in Medicare Part A at the time of the transplant.
    Cy is enrolled in Medicare Part B at the time the drugs are dispensed.
    the labeling of the tacrolimus includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ.
    the finding regimen necessary to prevent rejection about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    claim 2 is for the other tacrolimus.
    the HCPCS code of the other tacrolimus is "J7507".
    the other tacrolimus is furnished to Dee.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the diagnosis code of Dee is "Z94.83".
    Dee received a transplant of pancreas alone on 2024-05-10.
    the transplant of Dee was performed in a facility that is Medicare approved for kidney transplantation.
    the medical record of Dee documents type I diabetes.
    the fasting C-peptide level of Dee is 150 percent of the lower limit of normal.
    the fasting glucose of Dee obtained with the C-peptide determination is 180 mg per dl.
    the medical record of Dee documents labile insulin dependent diabetes with hospitalization.
    Dee was under the care of an endocrinologist with optimal and intensive management for 18 months.
    the finding able to manage lifelong immunosuppression about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding suitable candidate for transplantation about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the transplant of Dee met the Medicare coverage criteria in effect at the time.
    Dee was enrolled in Medicare Part A at the time of the transplant.
    Dee is enrolled in Medicare Part B at the time the drugs are dispensed.
    the labeling of the other tacrolimus includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ.
    the finding regimen necessary to prevent rejection about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

