    rn expects answers [].

% Parenteral drugs after a heart transplant (Z94.1): azathioprine injection
% (J7501) for Fay, who cannot absorb the oral form and self-administers it,
% is covered; belatacept (J0485) is denied in the home; and Gus's
% azathioprine injection, with no intolerance in the record, is not covered.
scenario parenteral_drugs is:
    claim 1 is for the azathioprine injection.
    the HCPCS code of the azathioprine injection is "J7501".
    the azathioprine injection is furnished to Fay.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the oral form of the azathioprine injection cannot be tolerated or absorbed by Fay.
    the azathioprine injection is self administered by the beneficiary.
    the diagnosis code of Fay is "Z94.1".
    Fay received a transplant of heart on 2025-09-15.
    the transplant of Fay met the Medicare coverage criteria in effect at the time.
    Fay was enrolled in Medicare Part A at the time of the transplant.
    Fay is enrolled in Medicare Part B at the time the drugs are dispensed.
    the labeling of the azathioprine injection includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ.
    the finding regimen necessary to prevent rejection about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    claim 2 is for the belatacept.
    the HCPCS code of the belatacept is "J0485".
    the belatacept is furnished to Fay.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the labeling of the belatacept includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ.
    claim 3 is for the other azathioprine injection.
    the HCPCS code of the other azathioprine injection is "J7501".
    the other azathioprine injection is furnished to Gus.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Gus is "Z94.1".
    Gus received a transplant of heart on 2025-09-15.
    the transplant of Gus met the Medicare coverage criteria in effect at the time.
    Gus was enrolled in Medicare Part A at the time of the transplant.
    Gus is enrolled in Medicare Part B at the time the drugs are dispensed.
    the labeling of the other azathioprine injection includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ.
    the finding regimen necessary to prevent rejection about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A refill of a 90-day supply of tacrolimus a year after the transplant,
% affirmed eight days before the current supply ends and delivered four
% days before: payable — the transplant establishes the continued need, no
% record of continued need or use is required.
scenario tacrolimus_refill is:
    claim 1 is for the tacrolimus.
    the HCPCS code of the tacrolimus is "J7507".
    the tacrolimus is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    claim 1 is a refill.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2027-02-25.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "Z94.0".
    Ann received a transplant of kidney on 2026-02-20.
    the transplant of Ann met the Medicare coverage criteria in effect at the time.
    Ann was enrolled in Medicare Part A at the time of the transplant.
    Ann is enrolled in Medicare Part B at the time the drugs are dispensed.
    Ann was discharged from the hospital following the transplant on 2026-03-01.
    the labeling of the tacrolimus includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ.
    the finding regimen necessary to prevent rejection about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the supplier holds the transplant date of Ann obtained from the treating practitioner.
    the current supply of the tacrolimus is expected to end on 2027-03-01.
    the beneficiary affirmed the need for the refill of the tacrolimus on 2027-02-21.
    the order for the tacrolimus is dated 2026-02-27.
    the order for the tacrolimus is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the tacrolimus includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the tacrolimus includes order date.
    the order for the tacrolimus includes description of the item.
    the order for the tacrolimus includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the tacrolimus includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the tacrolimus was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-27.
    the tacrolimus was delivered on 2027-02-25.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the tacrolimus.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

