% The regimen and the finding. Hal: the Council finds the regimen
% unsupported (a dose outside accepted practice) — not reasonable and
% necessary. Ivy: nobody has made the finding — the answer is conditional on
% it.
scenario regimen_findings is:
    claim 1 is for the sirolimus.
    the HCPCS code of the sirolimus is "J7520".
    the sirolimus is furnished to Hal.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Hal is "Z94.2".
    Hal received a transplant of lung on 2025-06-01.
    the transplant of Hal met the Medicare coverage criteria in effect at the time.
    Hal was enrolled in Medicare Part A at the time of the transplant.
    Hal is enrolled in Medicare Part B at the time the drugs are dispensed.
    the labeling of the sirolimus includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ.
    the finding regimen necessary to prevent rejection about Hal is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the order is for a dose four times the labeled maintenance dose with no explanation in the record".
    claim 2 is for the other sirolimus.
    the HCPCS code of the other sirolimus is "J7520".
    the other sirolimus is furnished to Ivy.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Ivy is "Z94.2".
    Ivy received a transplant of lung on 2025-06-01.
    the transplant of Ivy met the Medicare coverage criteria in effect at the time.
    Ivy was enrolled in Medicare Part A at the time of the transplant.
    Ivy is enrolled in Medicare Part B at the time the drugs are dispensed.
    the labeling of the other sirolimus includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding regimen necessary to prevent rejection about Ivy is established"].
